  {
    "id": 3924308552,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "A breach needs to stop a surface hull immediately. This branch makes `vessel_max_speed()` zero, but `vessel_movement_tick_one()` still calls `vessel_sail_tick()`, which decelerates the current `ship->speed` by only the class acceleration and then advances `speed / 90` rooms. For example, a warship holed at speed 17 moves at speed 15.5 on the next tick and can cross several room edges before stopping; a hull holed on two sides also keeps moving while its sink timer runs. This violates S3 3.3.3 (one breach immobilizes; a sinking hull cannot move). Clear current speed or prevent travel as soon as the breach/sinking state starts.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
    },
