  {
    "id": 3924309923,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "The remaining sink time is runtime-only even though damaged hull condition is persisted. On boot, `load_all_ship_interiors()` calls `vessel_update_condition()` for a two-breach hull, which rolls a new 75\u2013150 second (owned) or 1000\u20131500 second (unowned) timer. A ship saved with one second left therefore gets a full new countdown after a normal restart; repeated restarts can keep it afloat indefinitely. S3 3.3.3 promises a bounded time from the second breach to sinking. Persist the deadline or remaining ticks and restore it without rerolling.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
