  {
    "id": 3924605727,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "Fixed in 55d883020. `vessel_update_condition()` runs after every hit (`vessel_resolve_hit()`, `vessel_apply_damage()`) and at load; it now zeroes `ship->speed` for a sinking hull and for one holed afloat, so neither carries her way into the next `vessel_sail_tick()`. A hull aloft with one hole keeps half speed, as 3.3.3 says. `Test_vessel_one_breach_immobilizes_and_two_sink` holes a warship at speed 17 and asserts speed 0 at once, the speed kept aloft, and 0 again when the second hole starts her sinking aloft.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
