  {
    "id": 3924606069,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "Fixed in 05b40a93b. `ship_runtime_state.sink_ticks` holds the remaining ticks. Phase 19 is not released yet, so the column joins it (schema, rollback, verifier, boot DDL, `master_schema.sql`) rather than a new phase. `vessel_db_save_runtime()` writes it with the hull's damage, and `vessel_db_load_runtime()` restores it before `load_all_ship_interiors()` calls `vessel_update_condition()`, which then finds her already sinking and does not reroll. I kept remaining ticks rather than a deadline because the countdown is a tick counter everywhere else and the holes it depends on are saved on the same row. The DB case in `Test_vessel_legacy_snapshot_converts_once_at_load` saves a hull holed on two sides with 3 ticks left, reloads and reconciles her, and asserts 3; without the fix it reads a rerolled 2033.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
    },
